        <briefdescription>
<para>Open a task and return an Arrow C stream for its projected live rows. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>When <ref refid="structiceberg_1_1FileScanTaskReader_1_1Options_1a110242cc2d0c8421a8760cfd4a061169" kindref="member">Options::apply_residuals</ref> is set, <ref refid="structiceberg_1_1FileScanTaskReader_1_1Options_1a07fc7c34e0484ecec603e835d2ad8792" kindref="member">Options::projected_schema</ref> must contain all fields referenced by the task&apos;s original residual. Missing references cause <ref refid="classiceberg_1_1FileScanTaskReader_1a5bc4ec48bcb4b53c1f74ad25ac32ffd7" kindref="member">Open()</ref> to fail; they are not added from the table schema. Rows are filtered after deletes and before final projection.</para>
<para>Partial tasks are supported for Parquet, with each row group assigned to the half-open range containing its midpoint, as in Java Iceberg. Row positions and inherited row IDs remain relative to the whole file. Other formats require whole-file tasks. The task and its shared data/delete-file metadata must not be mutated while the stream uses them. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
